-- title:
--   Descent of an absolutely irreducible residual representation to a finite subfield
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and $k_0 \subseteq k$ a subfield which is finite. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is: a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V = 2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho \colon \operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q}) \to \operatorname{End}_k(V)$ which factors through a finite level, in the sense that there is an intermediate field $L$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with $L/\mathbb Q$ finite such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise is sent to the identity. Assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, meaning that in the base change of $\bar\rho$ to $\overline{k}$ the only submodules stable under all the operators $\bar\rho(\sigma) \otimes 1$ are $\bot$ and $\top$. Assume further that for every $\sigma \in \operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ and every $i \in \mathbb N$, the $i$-th coefficient of the characteristic polynomial of the $k$-linear endomorphism $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ lies in $k_0$. Then there exists a residual Galois representation $\bar\rho_0$ over $k_0$ (so a two-dimensional $k_0$-space carrying such a homomorphism factoring through a finite level) whose base change along the inclusion $k_0 \hookrightarrow k$ is equivalent to $\bar\rho$: there is a $k$-linear isomorphism $k \otimes_{k_0} V_0 \xrightarrow{\sim} V$ intertwining $\bar\rho_0(\sigma) \otimes 1$ with $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ for every $\sigma$. No uniqueness of $\bar\rho_0$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the descent of the coefficient field of an absolutely irreducible two-dimensional residual representation to the finite subfield generated by its characteristic polynomial coefficients; over a finite field the relevant Schur index is $1$, the Brauer group being trivial. It is used in the construction of the Galois representation attached to a cusp form, in [`CuspForm.exists_heckeGaloisRepDatum_pi_eq_and_isUnramifiedAt_of_forall_ringHom_exists_galoisRepAdic`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_heckeGaloisRepDatum_pi_eq_and_isUnramifiedAt_of_forall_ringHom_exists_galoisRepAdic), to realise the residual representation over the field generated by the Hecke eigenvalues mod $p$.
